 No configuration is needed.
 
+## Menu links rebuild
+
+The menu links are rebuilt when entities like menus, roles, views or bundles
+(content types, etc.) are created, updated or deleted. To avoid hundreds of
+rebuilds, for example when installing modules, the rebuild is deferred: all the
+requests are collected and a single rebuild is done before the response is sent
+to the client (`kernel.response` event) or at the end of the request (Drush).
+
+Code saving these entities programmatically sees the previous menu links until
+then. Tests saving them in the test process have to flush the pending rebuild
+with `\Drupal::service('admin_toolbar_tools.menu_link_rebuild_manager')->destruct()`.
+
 ## Maintainers
 
 Current maintainers:
